/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 48 0 R
/T (Low-code platforms allow applications to be developed mainly through visual development tools instead of writing large amounts of traditional program code. Applications are assembled using predefined components such as forms, reports and dashboards, and behaviour is defined through workflows, rules and configuration. A small amount of scripting is usually available for specific needs. This approach reduces development time and effort and makes it possible for a wider range of people to take part in building business applications.)
/E (Low-code platforms allow applications to be developed mainly through visual development tools instead of writing large amounts of traditional program code. Applications are assembled using predefined components such as forms, reports and dashboards, and behaviour is defined through workflows, rules and configuration. A small amount of scripting is usually available for specific needs. This approach reduces development time and effort and makes it possible for a wider range of people to take part in building business applications.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [17]
>>
